All right.  Go check out the last ttyrec for player Tenaya on NAO.

HJC, I hope that you appreciate this because it meant that I had to
redirect an existing game but if it serves to educate, then I'll be
satisfied.

The ttyrec starts with me hiding behing a boulder with a stack of 102
rocks.  I had created a pit alley in the non-aligned Minetown temple
with the priest trapped on the altar or one away but still
orthogonal.  Please appreciate that I could have killed him the easy
way with a polymorphed pet but wanted to illustrate that there are
multiple ways to kill the Minetown priest (and I didn't need to be a
wizard or have MR or have a ring of polymorph control or even find a
polymorph trap).

Here is my setup
..@..
--0--
.^H^.
.^@^.
.^.^.
where the top @ is me, the 0 is a boulder (because I couldn't get out
of summon insect range), the H is a hole, the ^ are pits, the lower @
is the priest on the altar

Anyhow, the priest and 2 other monsters died to the rock barrage.
Then I dug a pit in front of Izchak's shop, grabbed a candle, and
teleported out.  Here is where the supposed "abuse" breaks down.  Kops
are really stupid, forget webs!  I practically needed to build a
conveyor belt to get them to follow me!  It was like twisting their
arms!  It took an agonizing amount of turns but I managed to lead
about a dozen Kops onto the altar.  The first corpse converted the
altar and the second two summoned Juiblex and Yeenoghu.  The second
annoyance was that corpses are not always left.

But with another 6 or 7 Kop corpses I got 3 incubus and 4 succubus and
gained 9 experience levels.  Yay...meh...
In my opinion, with the exception of getting to XP=14 so that I can go
on the quest, spending extra time leveling up is just that, extra
time.  As for whether or not Kop farming on a chaotic human altar is
abusive, I suppose it is a matter of opinion, but I certainly
considered it to be abusive on my eyes for having to stare at the
screen (not to mention the induced mind-numbing!)

If you want to polymorph such and such and spin webs and acquire Sting
just to add levels of complexity to your game, that's your
prerogative, but for this scenario the only "abuse" arises from
applying a pick-axe and thowing rocks.

